[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A TLS listener decides whether to request a client certificate during the handshake,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"before it has seen any HTTP, so “ask for a certificate on ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/oauth2\/token","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" but not on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\/oauth2\/authorize","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"” is not something one listener can do. A deployment wanting both runs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"two, and this object names the second.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only these seven are ever aliased. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"authorization_endpoint"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"end_session_endpoint"},{"type":"text","text":" are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"front-channel and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jwks_uri"},{"type":"text","text":" is public key material, so §21.3 rule 2 forbids synthesising"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an alias for any of them — sending a browser to an mTLS host raises a native"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"certificate-chooser dialog most users cannot answer. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"issuer"},{"type":"text","text":" is not an endpoint and does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not move either: §12.4 rule 3 still compares "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iss"},{"type":"text","text":" against it by exact string."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every property is optional"}]},{"type":"text","text":", though the server’s schema marks them required. AXIAM"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"builds them from one path through a shared macro and so always publishes the complete set,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"but RFC 8705 §5 permits an OP to alias fewer, and the shape of this member must never be"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"why a client stops working — the same principle rule 2 point 1 states for the object as a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whole, one level in. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" entry falls back to the top-level endpoint of the same name,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exactly as an absent object does."}]}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"RFC 8705 §5 ","type":"text"},{"code":"mtls_endpoint_aliases","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — the seven endpoints re-based on the host that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"performs the mutual-TLS handshake (wire schema ","type":"text"},{"code":"MtlsEndpointAliases","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", contract 1.40; the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"seventh, CIBA’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"backchannel_authentication_endpoint","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", joined in contract 1.58).","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/mtlsendpointaliases"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/Se","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SQ","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo"}],"references":{"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/MtlsEndpointAliases/init(from:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/MtlsEndpointAliases\/init(from:)","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/mtlsendpointaliases\/init(from:)","abstract":[],"role":"symbol","title":"init(from:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s7DecoderP","